Package: baxters-remotedexter
Version: 3.1.0.2-1
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Baxter <baxtersbeats@outlook.com>
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libatomic1, libffi8, libglib2.0-0t64,
 libgstreamer1.0-0, libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-0, liborc-0.4-0t64,
 libpcre2-8-0, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-pipewire,
 xdg-desktop-portal, pipewire
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-gtk | xdg-desktop-portal-kde
Conflicts: remotedexter (<< 3.1.0~)
Replaces: remotedexter (<< 3.1.0~)
Provides: remotedexter
Description: Remote desktop host for Wayland, driven from an Android phone
 RemoteDexter shares this machine's desktop with a paired Android device over a
 Noise XX channel with the host's identity key pinned client-side. Capture is
 Wayland-native through xdg-desktop-portal and PipeWire; input injection uses
 the kernel's uinput virtual device, which no other display protocol on Wayland
 can provide.
 .
 Installing this package starts nothing and listens on nothing. There is no
 service, no autostart, no open port and no key until the host is launched and
 the operator presses Start. Input injection needs /dev/uinput, and the grant
 for it is a separate, explicit, reversible action taken from the host UI -- the
 packaged udev rule ships as inert data and is never installed by the package.
 .
 This package replaces the standalone "remotedexter" package of the 3.0 series;
 installing it removes that package and takes over its command.
